# Visible-child lifecycle and user-owned cover

See `docs/architecture/UI_LIFECYCLE_AND_COVER_OWNERSHIP.md`.

## Visible child detach

Never `setParent(None)` on a **visible** `QWidget`. That maps a top-level HWND
and steals `MainWindow` focus (seen as `DependencyItem` after cover/refresh/offline
success). Sequence is `hide()` → `setParent(None)` → `deleteLater()` via
`ui.window_lifecycle.detach_owned_widget`.

Do not globally ban `setParent`, `show()`, or dialogs. Do not hide the flash
with sleep/timers. The Import-Mod `show`/`setVisible` guard does **not** cover
detach.

## User-owned cover

User-set cover (`apply_cover_to_mod` + `user_override_fields.cover`) is not
refresh-fetched cover. Generic refresh / sidecar rescan must not point
`mods.cover_path` at a stale absolute path, official preview, backup blob, or
placeholder. Do not clobber in-memory `cover_path` in `_build_unified_payload`
with a pre-update sidecar snapshot.

## UI refresh

Do not sync Detail by adding extra `show_mod()` rebuilds. One logical mutation
uses `_canonical_detail_sync` and one `_reload_current_detail_from_projection`.
Success paths must not create unrequested top-level UI or launch Explorer.

## Production mutation boundary

Cover, metadata, backup, and deploy writes require
`services.mutation_context`. Test and forensic code must pass an explicit
temporary root. Production context is activated only from `main._run_gui`.
No context refuses the write. Do not fall back to the current library or
the first visible Mod. Do not treat a path prefix such as a drive letter
as the boundary.

## Regression gate

Not Cursor-specific. See `AGENTS.md`. After touching `show_mod`,
`notify_mod_changed`, `setParent`, `cover_path`, `apply_sidecar_to_db`, or
`_build_unified_payload`, run:

`python -m pytest tests/test_success_path_ui_invariants.py tests/test_cover_ownership_invariants.py tests/test_widget_detach_lifecycle.py tests/test_ui_lifecycle_static_guard.py`
